<article class="env-lemma" id="0DAC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DAC">Lemma <span data-tag="0DAC">85.22.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site with fibre products and $X \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$. Let $\mathcal{O}_\mathcal {C}$ be a sheaf of rings. Let $U$ be a hypercovering of $X$ in $\mathcal{C}$. For $E \in D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ the map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  E \longrightarrow Ra_*La^*E  \]
</div>
  <p> is an isomorphism. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a special case of Lemma <a href="/tag/0DA5" data-tag="0DA5">85.20.2</a>. 
